{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Silly Superstitions", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "No Umbrellas Inside", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 17, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe complicated or unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Be Supposed to", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "To talk about expectations, obligations or arrangements we can use the structure <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> . <span class=\"strong\">Be supposed to</span>  is used to talk about situations in the past, present or future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "This is the structure:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "subject + to be + supposed to + verb", "type": "text"}, {"content": "  <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">were supposed to</span> carve the pumpkin yesterday.<br/> I <span class=\"strong\">was supposed to</span> buy a costume last week.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I was supposed to decorate my house last week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You were supposed to help me carve pumpkins.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I was supposed to buy a Halloween costume.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They were supposed to go dancing.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Conditional Sentences with <span class=\"italic\">If</span> Clause", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">first conditional</span> with if clauses to exchange opinions about possible future outcomes, and to say it's possible that you will or will not do something.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">second conditional</span> to exchange opinions about unreal or imaginary (hypothetical) situations in the future, when there is no certainty that it's possible to fulfill the condition.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:  <br/><span class=\"italic\">If I won the lottery, I would buy a house.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Do you have a million dollars?  No.<br/> Is it possible to suddenly get a million dollars? Not really.<br/> What would you do if you had a million dollars? Buy a car.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"First Conditional:\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"First Conditional: 2nd Clause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> If I finish carving pumpkins, </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'll go to your house for dinner tonight.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's possible that I can go to dinner tonight, but only if I finish carving pumpkins. \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Second Conditional:<br/>If ... + Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Second Conditional: <br/>would + base verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> If I won the lottery, </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I would buy a big house</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It is impossible  and can only happen in a hypothetical situation.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "If we weren't good friends, I would be angry at him.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If I had a lot of money, I would buy a lot of pumpkins and donate them.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If they weren't a charity for kids, I would be more upset.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If I had a lot of money, I would donate money to charity.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to grab", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to take \u200bhold of something or someone \u200bsuddenly ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Yesterday, I grabbed an umbrella and opened it inside.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about Halloween.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to freak out", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to \u200bbecome \u200bextremely \u200bemotional", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(phrasal verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I opened an umbrella inside and one of my friends freaked out.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bunch", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a \u200bnumber of things of the same \u200btype", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was supposed to read a bunch of emails this week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "fitted", "type": "name"}, {"content": " made to \u200bfit the \u200bshape of someone or something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I had to get fitted for my Halloween costume. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to carve", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to \u200bcut into the \u200bsurface of \u200bstone, \u200bwood, a pumpkin, meat, etc.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I had to carve some pumpkins.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to take up", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to use up all or most of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(phrasal verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I had to do it and it took up a lot of time. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "charity", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a \u200bsystem of giving \u200bmoney, \u200bfood, or \u200bhelp to those who are in need", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If I had a lot of money, I would buy a lot of pumpkins and donate them to a local charity.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob07aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "It is Halloween, and you have lots to do, but you are very busy.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use \u201c supposed to\" and \"not supposed to \u201c to make a list of 5 sentences about all the things you need to do, but didn't do.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Then use \"If I had ... \" to talk about all the things you would do if you had more time.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compare  your lists with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Edit each other's sentences.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about manners, customs and superstitions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about things I was \"supposed to\" and \"not supposed to\" do and things that were \"supposed to\" happen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about hypothetical situations.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I edit other people's work.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"con